#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:2
msgid "The radio and the link layer"
msgstr "Radio i sloj veze"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:4
msgid ""
"The bottom two layers of the BLE stack are almost entirely automatic from "
"Python's perspective -- the radio silicon and the layers MicroPython runs on"
" top of it handle everything from picking a channel to retransmitting a lost"
" packet. Three of the choices they make still show through into the user-"
"facing API: power, range, and throughput."
msgstr ""
"Donja dva sloja BLE stoga gotovo su u potpunosti automatska iz Pythonove "
"perspektive -- radio silicij i slojevi koje MicroPython pokreće na njemu "
"obavljaju sve, od odabira kanala do ponovnog slanja izgubljenog paketa. Tri "
"odluke koje donose ipak se probijaju u API vidljiv korisniku: snaga, domet i"
" propusnost."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:13
msgid "The radio"
msgstr "Radio"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:15
msgid ""
"BLE uses the same 2.4 GHz Industrial-Scientific-Medical (ISM) band as Wi-Fi,"
" microwave ovens, and most other short-range wireless. The band is split "
"into 40 channels 2 MHz wide."
msgstr ""
"BLE koristi isti 2,4 GHz Industrijsko-znanstveno-medicinski (ISM) pojas kao "
"Wi-Fi, mikrovalne pećnice i većina drugih bežičnih veza kratkog dometa. "
"Pojas je podijeljen na 40 kanala širine 2 MHz."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Three** of the 40 channels are reserved for *advertising* -- short "
"broadcasts that announce a device's presence to anyone listening. They are "
"spaced out across the band so a listener can sweep all three quickly and so "
"interference on any one is unlikely to knock the device off the air "
"entirely."
msgstr ""
"**Tri** od 40 kanala rezervirana su za *oglašavanje* -- kratke emisije koje "
"objavljuju prisutnost uređaja svakome tko sluša. Razmaknuti su preko cijelog"
" pojasa kako bi slušatelj mogao brzo pretražiti sva tri i kako bi smetnje na"
" bilo kojem od njih malo vjerojatno potpuno izbacile uređaj iz etera."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:26
msgid ""
"**Thirty-seven** are *data* channels. Once two devices connect, they "
"exchange packets on these, hopping between them on a pseudo-random sequence "
"the two sides agree on at connection time. *Adaptive frequency hopping* lets"
" either side mark a channel as bad (heavy Wi-Fi interference, microwave, "
"neighbouring BLE network) so the sequence skips it."
msgstr ""
"**Trideset i sedam** su *podatkovni* kanali. Kada se dva uređaja povežu, "
"razmjenjuju pakete na njima, skačući između njih po pseudonasumičnom slijedu"
" koji obje strane dogovore u trenutku uspostave veze. *Prilagodljivo "
"frekvencijsko skakanje* omogućuje bilo kojoj strani da označi kanal kao loš "
"(jake Wi-Fi smetnje, mikrovalna pećnica, susjedna BLE mreža) tako da ga "
"slijed preskoči."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:34
msgid ""
"A horizontal frequency axis from 2400 MHz to\n"
"2480 MHz with 40 narrow channel slots drawn on\n"
"it. Three of the slots, at the bottom edge,\n"
"middle, and upper edge of the band, are\n"
"highlighted as \"advertising channels\". The\n"
"remaining 37 are labelled \"data channels\"."
msgstr ""
"Vodoravna frekvencijska os od 2400 MHz do\n"
"2480 MHz s 40 uskih utora kanala iscrtanih na\n"
"njoj. Tri utora, na donjem rubu, sredini i\n"
"gornjem rubu pojasa, istaknuta su kao\n"
"\"advertising channels\". Preostalih 37 označeno\n"
"je kao \"data channels\"."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:34
msgid ".. image:: ../figures/advertising-channels.svg"
msgstr ".. image:: ../figures/advertising-channels.svg"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:42
msgid ""
"The 40 BLE channels on the 2.4 GHz band. Three are for advertising, the rest"
" carry traffic on an open connection."
msgstr ""
"40 BLE kanala na 2,4 GHz pojasu. Tri su za oglašavanje, ostatak nosi promet "
"na otvorenoj vezi."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:46
msgid ""
"The radio transmits brief packets -- at most a couple of milliseconds long "
"-- and sleeps in between. That sleep is what makes the technology *low "
"energy*. A typical BLE peripheral spends well under one percent of its time "
"actually transmitting; the rest is the radio powered down between scheduled "
"events."
msgstr ""
"Radio odašilje kratke pakete -- najviše par milisekundi duge -- i spava "
"između njih. Taj san je ono što tehnologiju čini *niskoenergetskom*\\ . "
"Tipičan BLE peripheral provodi znatno manje od jedan posto svog vremena u "
"stvarnom odašiljanju; ostatak je radio isključen između zakazanih događaja."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:54
msgid "The link layer"
msgstr "Sloj veze"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:56
msgid ""
"The link layer is the smallest unit of BLE that talks to its counterpart on "
"another device. It handles four jobs."
msgstr ""
"Sloj veze najmanja je jedinica BLE-a koja razgovara sa svojim parnjakom na "
"drugom uređaju. Obavlja četiri posla."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:59
msgid ""
"**Packet framing.** Each packet carries a short header (channel access "
"address, packet length, control bits), a payload, and a CRC. The receiver "
"checks the CRC and drops anything corrupted."
msgstr ""
"**Uokvirivanje paketa.** Svaki paket nosi kratko zaglavlje (adresa pristupa "
"kanalu, duljina paketa, kontrolni bitovi), korisni teret i CRC. Primatelj "
"provjerava CRC i odbacuje sve oštećeno."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:63
msgid ""
"**Addressing.** Every BLE device has a 48-bit *device address* that "
"identifies it on the radio. Some are *public* -- a hardware identifier the "
"manufacturer has assigned, traceable forever. Some are *random* -- generated"
" on the device, rotated periodically, and optionally encrypted so that an "
"eavesdropper cannot link two transmissions to the same physical hardware. "
"Addresses come up again in "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/gap/advertising-and-scanning`."
msgstr ""
"**Adresiranje.** Svaki BLE uređaj ima 48-bitnu *adresu uređaja* koja ga "
"identificira na radiju. Neke su *javne* -- hardverski identifikator koji je "
"proizvođač dodijelio, sljediv zauvijek. Neke su *nasumične* -- generirane na"
" uređaju, povremeno rotirane i opcionalno šifrirane tako da prisluškivač ne "
"može povezati dva odašiljanja s istim fizičkim hardverom. Adrese se ponovno "
"spominju u :doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/gap/advertising-and-"
"scanning`\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:72
msgid ""
"**Connection scheduling.** Once two devices connect, the link layer "
"schedules periodic radio events on the hopping sequence -- a fixed "
"*connection interval* apart -- and packs whatever data is queued from the "
"GATT layer above into each one. Both sides go back to sleep between events. "
"The connection interval is a knob the application can request (see "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/gap/connections`)."
msgstr ""
"**Raspoređivanje veze.** Kada se dva uređaja povežu, sloj veze raspoređuje "
"periodične radio događaje na slijedu skakanja -- na razmaku fiksnog "
"*intervala veze* -- i pakira u svaki od njih sve podatke koji su u redu "
"čekanja iz GATT sloja iznad. Obje strane vraćaju se na spavanje između "
"događaja. Interval veze je regulator koji aplikacija može zatražiti (vidi "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/gap/connections`\\ )."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:80
msgid ""
"**Reliability.** Each packet on a connection is acknowledged by the other "
"side. The link layer retransmits anything that did not get a response, so "
"the layers above see an ordered, lossless byte stream. Unlike "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/networking/transport/udp` on the networking side, "
"BLE does not have a separate unreliable mode in normal use -- every packet "
"on an open connection is retried until it arrives or the link is declared "
"lost."
msgstr ""
"**Pouzdanost.** Svaki paket na vezi potvrđuje druga strana. Sloj veze "
"ponovno šalje sve što nije dobilo odgovor, tako da slojevi iznad vide "
"uređeni tok bajtova bez gubitaka. Za razliku od "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/networking/transport/udp` na strani umrežavanja, "
"BLE u uobičajenoj upotrebi nema zaseban nepouzdan način rada -- svaki paket "
"na otvorenoj vezi ponovno se pokušava poslati dok ne stigne ili dok se veza "
"ne proglasi izgubljenom."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:90
msgid ""
"The link layer is also where *encryption* runs once a pair of devices has "
"agreed on a key during pairing (see "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/security/pairing-and-bonding`). Every "
"packet on an encrypted link is decrypted at the receiver before the layers "
"above ever see it."
msgstr ""
"Sloj veze također je mjesto gdje se *šifriranje* odvija kada se par uređaja "
"dogovorio o ključu tijekom sparivanja (vidi "
":doc:`/openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/security/pairing-and-bonding`\\ ). Svaki"
" paket na šifriranoj vezi dešifrira se na primatelju prije nego što ga "
"slojevi iznad uopće vide."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:98
msgid "What the camera and a peer share"
msgstr "Što kamera i suparnik dijele"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:100
msgid ""
"The radios on both ends agree at connection time on a handful of parameters "
"that govern the conversation:"
msgstr ""
"Radiji na oba kraja u trenutku uspostave veze dogovaraju se o nekolicini "
"parametara koji upravljaju razgovorom:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:103
msgid ""
"The *connection interval* -- how often the two sides wake up to exchange "
"packets, anywhere from 7.5 ms to 4 s."
msgstr ""
"*Interval veze* -- koliko se često dvije strane bude da razmijene pakete, "
"bilo gdje od 7,5 ms do 4 s."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:106
msgid ""
"The *peripheral latency* -- how many consecutive intervals the peripheral "
"may skip if it has nothing to say, to save power."
msgstr ""
"*Latencija peripherala* -- koliko uzastopnih intervala peripheral smije "
"preskočiti ako nema što reći, radi uštede energije."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:109
msgid ""
"The *supervision timeout* -- how long either side waits before declaring the"
" link lost when the other goes quiet."
msgstr ""
"*Nadzorno vrijeme isteka* -- koliko dugo bilo koja strana čeka prije nego "
"što proglasi vezu izgubljenom kada druga utihne."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:112
msgid ""
"The *MTU* -- the largest single packet either side will deliver to GATT "
"(defaults to 23 bytes, can be negotiated up)."
msgstr ""
"*MTU* -- najveći pojedinačni paket koji će bilo koja strana isporučiti "
"GATT-u (zadano 23 bajta, može se pregovorom povećati)."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:116
msgid ""
"The radio and the link layer together are responsible for getting reliable, "
"ordered packets from one device to another while keeping both radios off as "
"much as possible. Every layer above is free to behave as if a clean, private"
" byte channel exists between the two endpoints."
msgstr ""
"Radio i sloj veze zajedno odgovorni su za dostavu pouzdanih, uređenih paketa"
" s jednog uređaja na drugi, uz držanje oba radija isključenima što je više "
"moguće. Svaki sloj iznad slobodan je ponašati se kao da između dvije krajnje"
" točke postoji čist, privatan kanal bajtova."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:124
msgid "What Python sees of all this"
msgstr "Što Python vidi od svega ovoga"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/bluetooth/radio/physical-and-link.rst:126
msgid ""
"Almost nothing. The :mod:`bluetooth` and :mod:`aioble` APIs do not expose "
"channels, hopping sequences, packet CRCs, or retransmission timers; those "
"are all handled inside the BLE port and the radio. The pieces that *do* show"
" through are the ones the connection-time negotiation exposes -- connection "
"interval, MTU, address type."
msgstr ""
"Gotovo ništa. API-ji :mod:`bluetooth` i :mod:`aioble` ne izlažu kanale, "
"slijedove skakanja, CRC-ove paketa ili mjerače vremena ponovnog slanja; sve "
"to obrađuje se unutar BLE porta i radija. Dijelovi koji se *probijaju* su "
"oni koje izlaže pregovor u trenutku uspostave veze -- interval veze, MTU, "
"vrsta adrese."
